; The ONE variable: a [center] line WIDER than its own box. RichTextLabel draws
; its lines through its own alignment switch (rich_text_label.cpp:999-1014),
; whose CENTER arm is unguarded — unlike TextParagraph::draw's, which no-ops
; once the line overflows (text_paragraph.cpp:1004). The two disagree only on an
; overflowing line, so no other RichTextLabel fixture can tell which one this
; previewer transcribes. autowrap is OFF so the line cannot wrap out of the
; overflow. The box is 200 wide and centred, so its OWN rect mirror
; (control.cpp:1785) is the identity.

